# SPA fallback for the framework-port online routes (/lobby, /play/:id).
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves existing static assets and /api/* Functions FIRST,
# so this only catches client-side routes that have no file on disk.
#
# NOTE: a targeted rule like `/lobby /index.html 200` gets 308-redirected to
# `/` by Pages' "pretty URL" normalization (rewriting *to* /index.html is
# normalized to /), so /lobby fell through to the hotseat root. The catch-all
# splat below is the documented SPA pattern and is NOT normalized, so /lobby
# and /play/<id>?as=<tok> resolve to the app correctly.
/*    /index.html    200
